The attached image, Figure 2 from the npj Vaccines (2017) paper, illustrates the in vivo biodistribution and clearance kinetics of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles following intramuscular injection in mice. Panel a shows whole-mouse fluorescence imaging over 21 days, demonstrating Nano-11 retention at the injection site and gradual clearance. Panel b displays imaging of excised internal organs at day 21, confirming minimal systemic distribution. Panel c quantifies injection site fluorescence, showing an initial transient decrease (possibly due to edema) followed by a progressive reduction over three weeks, supporting that Nano-11 is confined to the injection area and eventually cleared.